hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"185","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told me, Abdullah bin Nafi told me, on the authority of Dawud. H Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam narrated to us, Abdullah bin Nafi’ narrated to us, Daoud bin Qays narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata bin Yassar, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Bilal entered the markets, and he went for his needs. He said: Then They went out. Osama said: I asked Bilala what he had done. Bilal said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to relieve himself, then he performed ablution, washed his face and hands, wiped his head, and wiped over his socks.” . Yunus added in his hadith: “Then he prayed.” Abu Bakr said: The markets surround the city. He said: I heard Yunus, saying: “There is no news from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he wiped over “The socks in urban areas are other than this.”"
